'''''Wolverine and the X-Men''''' is an American [[Superhero fiction|superhero]] [[animated series]] produced by [[Marvel Studios]]. It is the fourth animated adaptation of the [[X-Men]] characters. In the show, [[Wolverine (character)|Wolverine]] attempts to reassemble the X-Men and becomes their new leader, following a devastating incident that led to the disappearances of both [[Jean Grey]] and [[Professor X|Charles Xavier]].

==Plot==
At the start of the series, the [[X-Men]] disband following an explosion that destroys the [[X-Mansion]] and causes [[Professor X]] and [[Jean Grey]] to disappear. One year later, [[Wolverine (character)|Wolverine]] and [[Beast (Marvel Comics)|Beast]] decide to reunite the X-Men after witnessing the rise of the [[Mutant Response Division]], a government-supported organization dedicated to capturing [[Mutant (Marvel Comics)|mutants]].

The X-Men receive funding from [[Warren Worthington III|Angel]] and reunite with junior members [[Iceman (Marvel Comics)|Iceman]], [[Kitty Pryde|Shadowcat]] and [[Forge (character)|Forge]]. However, the X-Men are unable to locate the group's other members without a competent [[telepath]] to operate [[Cerebro]]. [[Emma Frost]] arrives and volunteers to join the X-Men in exchange for helping them find Professor X. Frost finds Professor X on the shores of [[Genosha]] in the care of [[Magneto (Marvel Comics)|Magneto]]. After their arrival on Genosha, Magneto permits the X-Men to take Professor X into their care. Upon their return, Xavier telepathically contacts a future version of the X-Men, who originate from a dystopian future twenty years from the present.

Meanwhile, Magneto welcomes new mutants to Genosha, one of whom is [[Nightcrawler (character)|Nightcrawler]]. Magneto claims that Genosha is a safe and secure area for mutants, rather than a threat. Nightcrawler initially believes this, but later learns that Magneto is exploiting other mutants for power. Nightcrawler escapes, but is captured by [[Mystique (character)|Mystique]] when he arrives back at the mansion.

[[Cyclops (Marvel Comics)|Cyclops]] has constant memories about Jean Grey and is depressed. He believes she is still alive, so, with the help of Frost, he seeks out [[Mister Sinister]]. The X-Men and [[Mister Sinister]] have a confrontation that does not result in them finding out any new info about Jean's whereabouts. Wolverine has Cyclops swear an oath to be in the X-Men again and promise not to go off searching for Jean. Somewhere across town, Jean is shown waking up in a hospital after months of being in a coma.

In the series finale, "Foresight", it is revealed that the destruction of the X-Mansion was caused by Jean Grey, who had unknowingly unleashed the Phoenix Force while defending herself against a telepathic attack led by Emma Frost. However, Emma's true motivation was heroic: she sought to save both Jean Grey and the entire world from the destructive power of the [[Phoenix Force]]. She genuinely believed that the [[Hellfire Club (comics)|Inner Circle]] was an ancient organization that had protected the world from the Phoenix for generations, as demonstrated by her own explanation to Jean and the historical murals she showed her. Emma believed their mission was to separate the Phoenix Force from Jean and destroy it before it could threaten the world. Unbeknownst to her, the other members of the Inner Circle were actually villains who intended to control the Phoenix Force for their own purposes. Emma was shocked upon discovering their true intentions and was equally horrified when Selene suggested killing the X-Men, openly protesting, "Since when do we kill people? We're supposed to save lives, not take them!" Upon realizing that she had been deceived, Emma turned against the Inner Circle and ultimately sacrificed her own life to destroy the Phoenix Force, saving Jean Grey, the X-Men, and the entire world.

The now fully reformed X-Men are praised for their actions by Professor Xavier, but are warned that the initial future has been replaced with a new timeline dominated by [[Apocalypse (character)|Apocalypse]].

