==Production==
Toonz Animation India and First Serve International formed a joint venture Toonz First Serve to produce ''Wolverine''.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Bhushan |first1=Nyay |title=India's Toonz has claws out |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/indias-toonz-has-claws-135678 |access-date=May 20, 2019 |work=The Hollywood Reporter |agency=AP |date=May 8, 2007 |language=en}}</ref> By November 2007, Toonz First Serve began production on the series.

On November 4, 2008, a second season, consisting of 26 episodes was confirmed as being in production by Toonz Entertainment and Marvel Animation.<ref>{{cite news |title=Toonz, Marvel tie up for second part of X-Men series |url=http://www.thaindian.com/newsportal/sci-tech/toonz-marvel-tie-up-for-second-part-of-x-men-series_100126335.html |access-date=May 20, 2019 |work=Thaindian News |agency=Indo-Asian News Service |date=December 2, 2008 |archive-date=November 7, 2009 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091107203544/http://www.thaindian.com/newsportal/sci-tech/toonz-marvel-tie-up-for-second-part-of-x-men-series_100126335.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> During Comic Con 2009, images of season 2 were shown, consisting of [[Bastion (comics)|Bastion]], [[Cable (character)|Cable]], [[Colossus (character)|Colossus]], [[Deadpool]], [[Havok (character)|Havok]], [[Jubilee (character)|Jubilee]], and [[Magik]]. It was announced that these characters were to appear in season 2. Colossus was set to receive a reintroductory storyline and would have been a regular character in season 2. Joshua Fine also revealed that [[Holocaust (Marvel Comics)|Holocaust]], [[Sunfire (character)|Sunfire]], and [[Unus the Untouchable]] would have made appearances in season 2.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.facebook.com/notes/1-million-to-save-wolverine-and-the-x-men/interview-with-joshua-fine-associate-producerwriter-of-wolverine-and-the-x-men/208529275849072/|title=Interview with Joshua Fine, Associate Producer/Writer of WOLVERINE AND THE X-MEN|website=www.facebook.com}}</ref> Joshua Fine confirmed that [[Deadpool]] would have been in a Weapon X episode also featuring [[X-23|X-23 / Laura Kinney]], and other obscure characters.<ref name="youtube.com">
{{Citation|title=Joshua Fine Interview! Wolverine and the X-Men, Season 2 Scripts, & More!| date=17 November 2021 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yzc-Dz97YKg|language=en|access-date=2021-11-17}}</ref>

===Cancellation===
On April 13, 2010, Comics Continuum reported that (according to an inside source) a second season seemed very unlikely.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.comicscontinuum.com/stories/1004/13/index.htm |title=Comics Continuum by Rob Allstetter: Tuesday, April 13, 2010 |publisher=Comicscontinuum.com |access-date=2011-02-20}}</ref> On April 15, 2010, Marvel Animation Age confirmed the recent report that ''Wolverine and the X-Men'' would not be returning for a second season.<ref name="toonzone">{{cite web|url=http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=518 |title=Marvel Animation Age |publisher=Marvel.toonzone.net |date=2010-04-15 |access-date=2011-02-20 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131104131135/http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=518 |archive-date=November 4, 2013 }}</ref> The reason for this was due to financial problems with their financing partner.{{citation needed|date=March 2023}}

