==Broadcast history==
===United States===
On May 1, 2008, the show was pre-sold to [[Nicktoons Network]] in the United States and was set for a Spring 2009 airdate.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://kidscreen.com/2008/05/01/marvel-20080501/ | title=Marvel expands franchises with four new series and CP programs }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://forum.newsarama.com/showthread.php?t=147264 |title=MARVEL REPORTS Q4 2007 NUMBERS: PROFIT MORE THAN DOUBLES – NEWSARAMA |publisher=Forum.newsarama.com |access-date=2011-02-20 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090512233006/http://forum.newsarama.com/showthread.php?t=147264 |archive-date=2009-05-12 }}</ref> It was also confirmed in an article by [[USA Today]]'s website in which it specifically mentions the cartoon starting on January 23, 2009, on Nicktoons Network.<ref>{{cite web|last=Keveney |first=Bill |url=https://www.usatoday.com/life/television/news/2008-03-17-marvel-nicktoons_N.htm |title=Marvel superheroes power up for Nicktoons |publisher=Usatoday.com |date=2008-03-18 |access-date=2011-02-20}}</ref> On January 23, 2009, the show premiered in the United States, with the first two episodes shown back-to-back on Nicktoons Network, which were re-aired on [[Nickelodeon]] two days later. The next 6 episodes followed weekly before a two-month break. New episodes began on May 22, 2009, as advertised with commercials on the channel then stopped after June 19, 2009, till the network advertised that they will be showing new episodes on July 31, 2009, after or before new episodes of ''[[Iron Man: Armored Adventures]]''.

===United Kingdom===
On June 23, 2008, a second preview for the series, starring the main X-Men team, was released to announce the special screening of the 3-part pilot episodes that aired at [[San Diego Comic-Con]] in late July 2008.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://enewsi.com/news.php?catid=194&itemid=13507 |title=New Wolverine and the X-Men Trailer – Animation |publisher=ENewsI.com |date=2008-06-25 |access-date=2011-02-20 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110710192703/http://enewsi.com/news.php?catid=194&itemid=13507 |archive-date=2011-07-10 }}</ref> Press releases indicated that the first episode was due to premiere on August 2, 2008, on [[BBC Two]] in the UK, however, it was postponed and premiered on January 4, 2009,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b00gnfd6/upcoming |title=CBBC Programmes – Wolverine and The X-Men – Episodes coming up |publisher=BBC |access-date=2011-02-20 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090124030140/http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b00gnfd6/upcoming |archive-date=2009-01-24 }}</ref> on the [[CBBC|CBBC Channel]]. Initially, one new episode aired every Sunday, but on January 25, 2009, CBBC started airing two new episodes every Sunday. The time slots varied, and the episodes were available for viewing on the BBC iPlayer for a limited time after they aired. As of mid-February 2009, some new episodes were shown on weekdays instead of at the weekend. Some episodes with scenes showing heavy violence were censored and Episode 17 was not shown on CBBC as there was a duel to the death in the storyline (along with one scene depicting blood). CBBC in the UK overtook Canada on March 4, 2009, when it aired the 20th episode, "Breakdown.”

In 2009, [[BBC Alba]] started broadcasting the series dubbed into [[Scottish Gaelic]] as "An Sionnach Sgianach is Na Seòid".

The show later aired on [[Pop Max|Kix]], beginning in November 2013.

===Canada===
Early news had speculated the show to air in Fall 2008 in the United States.<ref>{{cite web |title=New X-Men Cartoon Early Fall 2008? |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080302104707/http://www.invertedstripes.com/index.php?subaction=showfull&id=1176213186&archive=&start_from=&ucat=& |url=http://www.invertedstripes.com/index.php?subaction=showfull&id=1176213186&archive=&start_from=&ucat=&|archive-date = 2008-03-02}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=11 |title=Marvel Animation Age |publisher=Marvel.toonzone.net |access-date=2011-02-20 |archive-date=June 8, 2008 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080608022951/http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=11 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.marvel.com/news/moviestories.1598.First_Look:_Wolverine~and~The_X-Men |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071012150021/http://marvel.com/news/moviestories.1598.First_Look:_Wolverine~and~The_X-Men |url-status=dead |archive-date=October 12, 2007 |title=First Look: Wolverine & The X-Men – Marvel.com News |publisher=Marvel.com |date=2007-09-26 |access-date=2011-02-20}}</ref> The series started airing on YTV on Saturday, September 6, 2008, in the 7:00&nbsp;p.m. time slot. When its time slot was switched to Saturday morning programming, Crunch, it aired at 11:30&nbsp;a.m. Starting in January 2009, the show was also shown on [[Cartoon Network (Canada)|Teletoon]], where only episodes that previously aired on YTV were shown.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.teletoon.com/teletoon3/teletoon.php?language=En&func=php|title=Teletoon show page|publisher=Teletoon.com|access-date=2011-02-20|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101023102742/http://www.teletoon.com/teletoon3/teletoon.php?language=en&func=php|archive-date=2010-10-23}}</ref>

===Latin America and Brazil===
In July 2008, the series was pre-sold to [[Disney XD (Latin America)|Jetix]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://kidscreen.com/2008/07/17/jetix-20080717/ | title=Jetix Latin America to air new Marvel toon }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://programacao.jetix.com.br/programacion/a-z_br.asp?letra=W&zona=16 |title=JETIX |access-date=2008-08-22 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090208155805/http://programacao.jetix.com.br/programacion/a-z_br.asp?letra=W&zona=16 |archive-date=2009-02-08 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://ww38.programacion.jetixtv.com/programacion/a-z.asp?letra=W&zona=8|title=jetixtv.com|website=ww38.programacion.jetixtv.com}}</ref> starting August 25, 2008 from Mondays to Thursdays at 4:30&nbsp;p.m.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.jetixtv.com/Series/Wolverine_Y_Los_X-Men/index.html |title=Disney XD – Inicio |publisher=Jetixtv.com |access-date=2011-02-20}}</ref> Unusually, all 26 episodes of the first season were aired in Brazil and Latin America before the series started in any other country. Also, the series airs in [[Record (TV network)|Rede Record]] in Brazil from Mondays to Fridays at 7:00&nbsp;p.m., starting November 9, 2009. In Mexico, the series aired on Azteca 7.

===Australia===
In Australia, the first series aired on [[ABC1]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.abc.net.au/abckids/guide/default_5.htm |title=ABC Kids TV guide |publisher=Abc.net.au |access-date=2011-02-20}}</ref> Sunday mornings. The series was then repeated weekdays in early morning and late afternoon timeslots. The show then aired on [[ABC Entertains|ABC3]], along with other series from [[Marvel Animation]] on Sunday nights.

==Merchandise==
[[Hasbro]] produced a Wolverine and the X-Men toyline as a tie-in to the series. The first wave consisted of [[Avalanche (character)|Avalanche]], [[Beast (Marvel Comics)|Beast]], [[Colossus (character)|Colossus]], [[Cyclops (Marvel Comics)|Cyclops]], Logan (not in classic outfit), [[Iceman (Marvel Comics)|Iceman]], [[Magneto (Marvel Comics)|Magneto]], and [[Wolverine (character)|Wolverine]]. Wave two contained the new figures [[Nightcrawler (character)|Nightcrawler]] and a Black Uniform Wolverine. Wave Three, the final wave, added [[Forge (character)|Forge]] and [[Toad (Marvel Comics)|Toad]] to the line. The toy line ended before any of the main females of the series were given toys; notably missing were [[Emma Frost]], [[Jean Grey]], [[Kitty Pryde|Shadowcat]], [[Rogue (Marvel Comics)|Rogue]], and [[Storm (Marvel Comics)|Storm]].

